---
servings: 16
---

== Dough

Mix @flour{390%g} and @dry yeast{7%g} in a big bowl. Add @milk{250%ml}(warmed to 37 degrees), @sugar{45%g}, @cardamom{0.5%tablespoon}, and @salt{0.5%teaspoon}.

Once mixed, add @butter{75%g}(room temperature) and mix further.

Knead for about ~{10%minutes} then cover with a wet cloth and let the dough rise for ~{1%hour}.

== Filling

While waiting, mix the filling: @butter{75%g}(room temperature), @sugar{45%g}, and @cinnamon{1%tablespoon}.

== Assembly

Spread the dough on a floured surface and roll it into a rectangle of about 25x50cm.

Add the filling evenly on top of the dough, then roll it up from the long side.

Cut the roll into 16 pieces and place them in a #baking dish{}. (cut side up where applicable)

Cover with a wet cloth and let rise for ~{30%minutes}.

== Baking

Mix @egg{1} for egg wash and brush it on top of the rolls.

Sprinkle @pearl sugar{}.

Warm #oven{} to 225°C and bake in the middle row for ~{8-10%minutes}.
